##DESCRIPTION
##  Algebra problem: Rewrite expression without using negative exponents
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('algebra', 'exponent', 'fraction')
## DBsubject(Algebra)
## DBchapter(Properties of exponents, rational exponents and radicals)
## DBsection(Properties of exponents)
## Level(2)
## Author(K. Andrew Parker)
## Institution(CUNY City Tech)
## Language(en)

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',    # Standard macros for PG language
    'PGML.pl',
    'contextFraction.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context("LimitedFraction")->flags->set(
    showMixedNumbers  => 0,
    reduceConstants   => 0,
    allowMixedNumbers => 0
);

Context()->{error}{msg}{"Can't use '^' in this context"} =
    "Exponents are disabled for this problem. Compute the result for yourself and resubmit your answer.";
Context()->{error}{msg}{"Can't use '**' in this context"} =
    "Exponents are disabled for this problem. Compute the result for yourself and resubmit your answer.";

$A    = Compute(random(4, 12));
$ansA = Fraction(1, $A**2);

$B    = Compute(random(4, 12));
$ansB = Fraction(-1, $B**2);

$C    = Compute(random(4, 12));
$ansC = Fraction(1, $C**2);

BEGIN_PGML

a) Rewrite [` [$A]^{-2} `] without using negative exponents.

    [_]{$ansA}

b) Rewrite [`` -[$B]^{-2} ``] without using negative exponents.

    [_]{$ansB}

c) Rewrite [``(-[$C])^{-2} ``] without using negative exponents.

    [_]{$ansC}
END_PGML

#  Answers

ANS($ansA->cmp);
ANS($ansB->cmp);
ANS($ansC->cmp);

BEGIN_PGML_HINT

Recall the exponent property: [` (B^{-1})^2 = B^{-2} `]

Do you remember what an exponent of -1 does? Apply the exponent of -1, then square your result...

END_PGML_HINT
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

a) [`` [$A]^{-2} = ([$A]^{-1})^2 = \left( \frac{1}{[$A]} \right)^2 = [$ansA] ``]
  
    OR
  
    [`` [$A]^{-2} = \frac{1}{[$A]^2} = [$ansA] ``]

b) Be careful! -[$B] is NOT in parenthesis, so [`` -[$B]^{-2} ``] means [`` -([$B]^{-2}) ``]!
  
    [`` -([$B]^{-2}) = -([$B]^{-1})^2 = -\left( \frac{1}{[$B]} \right)^2 = [$ansB] ``]

    OR

    [`` -([$B]^{-2}) = -\frac{1}{[$B]^2} = [$ansB] ``]

c) [`` (-[$C])^{-2} = ((-[$C])^{-1})^2 = \left( \frac{1}{-[$C]} \right)^2 = [$ansC] ``]

    OR

    [`` (-[$C])^{-2} = \frac{1}{(-[$C])^2} = [$ansC] ``]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

COMMENT("Funded by US DoE Title V: Opening Gateways grant.");

ENDDOCUMENT();        